   def run_game(self):

The second category in our Jungle Invasion class is our run_game line. This takes the role of reminding the computer to constantly reassess and run certain could should a condition become true.


def _check_events(self):


Part of the run_game functions job is the introduction of _check_events, which allows for movement. The idea here is by constantly checking the status of certain keys, (such as spacebar or the arrowkeys, the function can set certain movement / attack commands to true. Conversely, should the keyup check succeed, that movement command will halt, though it will ensure the player’s sprite appears looking in that direction. 

This pivots well into a final class I will mention, our Player class. 


class Player:
 def __init__(self, ai_game):
      self.facing = 'front'
      self.screen = ai_game.screen
      self.screen_rect = ai_game.screen.get_rect()
      self.attacking = False
      self.attack_timer = 0
      self.moving_right = self.moving_left = self.moving_up = self.moving_down = False

By creating a starting point, we are giving Python an understanding of how to process our character. As we start the game not attacking , nor looking in any direction, we manually set the self.facing to ‘front’ and self attacking to “False”. We mainly use the self.facing variable as a basis for generating images, where it will call to the frog facing left if self.facing_left = true, face down when self.facing_down = true, and vice versa. If multiple are true it will currently keep the image of the last facing direction. Once we hit the spacebar, self attacking is set to “True” and our movement halts until the attack animation is done. Python at this point will check for overlap with the enemy, ie, Goblin, “rect” or hitboxes. If there is an intersection, the goblin will disappear and trigger a “You’ve gotten one” text on the terminal. By setting an attack timer, we prevent a “spamming” of attacks and overlapping of multiple attack animations. The rule is, the Player must wait for the current attack timer to end in order to initiate an attack again.
 

